# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Energy Gurus Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version 1.4.1)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the complete dependency tree

### 2. Analytics Integration
- Modified `src/app/[locale]/layout.tsx` to integrate Vercel Analytics
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next'`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the root layout's body section

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I implemented the Next.js App Router pattern:

1. The Analytics component was added at the end of the `<body>` tag in the root layout
2. This placement ensures analytics tracking across all pages of the application
3. The implementation is framework-specific for Next.js App Router, using `@vercel/analytics/next`

## Files Modified

- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies
- `src/app/[locale]/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

## Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully with `npm run build`
- ✅ Linter ran successfully with no new errors introduced in modified files
- ✅ TypeScript compilation passed without errors
- ✅ No breaking changes to existing functionality

## Next Steps

To enable Web Analytics in production:
1. Deploy this code to Vercel
2. Navigate to your project's Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard
3. Click the "Enable" button to activate analytics tracking
4. After deployment, verify analytics are working by checking the Network tab for `/_vercel/insights/*` requests

The analytics will automatically start collecting data once enabled in the Vercel dashboard and the code is deployed.
